Here's a Dart function that takes a list of transaction objects and returns the top three coins with the highest average profit and the top 3 coins with highest average loss:

```dart
import 'package:collection/collection.dart';

List<Transaction> topCoinsWithHighestAverageProfit(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName);

  return groupedTransactions.entries
      .map((entry) => MapEntry(entry.key, entry.value.average((transaction) => transaction.profitEarned)))
      .toList()
      .sortBy((mapEntry) => mapEntry.value, reverse: true)
      .take(3);
}

List<Transaction> topCoinsWithHighestAverageLoss(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName);

  return groupedTransactions.entries
      .map((entry) => MapEntry(entry.key, entry.value.average((transaction) => transaction.profitLoss)))
      .toList()
      .sortBy((mapEntry) => mapEntry.value, reverse: true)
      .take(3);
}

class Transaction {
  final String coinName;
  final DateTime datetime;
  final double profitEarned;
  final double profitLoss;

  Transaction({required this.coinName, required this.datetime, required this.profitEarned, required this.profitLoss});
}
```

This function first groups the transactions by their coin name using the `groupBy` method from the `collection` package. It then calculates the average profit and average loss for each coin by iterating over the transactions in the corresponding group and summing up the profit earned or profit lost, respectively. Finally, it sorts the coins by their average profit or average loss in descending order and returns the top three coins for each category.

