To create a MATLAB program that converts a given phrase to its binary representation using the International Morse Code standard, follow these steps:

1. Define a function that takes a character as input and returns its Morse Code representation.

```matlab
function morse_code = get_morse_code(char)
    % Define the Morse Code representation for each character
    char_to_morse = {'.-', '-...', '-.-.', '-..', '.', '..-', '--.', '....', '..', '.---', '-.', '.-..', '--', '-.', '---', '.--.', '--.-', '.-', '...', '-', '..-', '...-', '.--', '-..-', '-.', '-.', '--..'};

    % Convert the character to uppercase
    char = upper(char);

    % Return the Morse Code representation for the character
    morse_code = char_to_morse{char};
end
```

2. Define a function that takes a phrase as input and returns its binary representation using the Morse Code standard.

```matlab
function binary_representation = convert_to_binary(phrase)
    % Initialize the binary representation
    binary_representation = '';

    % Iterate through each character in the phrase
    for i = 1:length(phrase)
        % Get the Morse Code representation for the current character
        morse_code = get_morse_code(phrase(i));

        % Add the Morse Code representation to the binary representation
        binary_representation = [binary_representation, morse_code];
    end

    % Remove any leading or trailing spaces from the binary representation
    binary_representation = trim(binary_representation);
end
```

3. Test the function with a sample phrase.

```matlab
phrase = 'Hello, World!';
binary_representation = convert_to_binary(phrase);
disp(binary_representation);
```

This program will output the binary representation of the input phrase using the International Morse Code standard.

